  "ref": "JER.6.16",
  "review_notes": [
    "The single 'the' of 'the good way' goes to the attributive's present article rather than to the anarthrous דֶרֶךְ (rule 47).",
    "אֵי־זֶה is aligned as one unit to 'where is' under rule 30's one-English-word condition, headed on אֵי; the earlier reading gave 'where is' to אֵי and marked זֶה unrepresented, which rule 30 rejects for a fixed multi-word expression the ASV renders with one word. JER.6.20's לָמָּה־זֶּה is the other side of the same condition and keeps its unrepresented זֶה."
  ]
